# SDD · Verify

The gate. No claim of success, no commit, no PR without **fresh** evidence from this run.

## The rule

> "Should pass" / "it works" / "looks good" **without cited output = a violation.**

A claim is valid only when you can cite, from the current state of the code:

- the command you ran,
- its output, and
- exit code 0 with zero errors (and zero warnings where the project treats warnings as
  errors).

Re-run the **full** pipeline after **any** fix before repeating a claim. Stale evidence
from before a change does not count.

## Pipeline

```bash
{% if task_runner == "just" -%}
just verify        # lint + typecheck + test
{% if e2e_cmd %}just e2e           # when the change touched runtime paths ({{ runtime_paths }})
{% endif -%}
{%- elif task_runner == "make" -%}
make verify        # lint + typecheck + test
{% if e2e_cmd %}make e2e           # when the change touched runtime paths ({{ runtime_paths }})
{% endif -%}
{%- elif task_runner == "npm" -%}
npm run verify     # lint + typecheck + test
{% if e2e_cmd %}npm run e2e        # when the change touched runtime paths ({{ runtime_paths }})
{% endif -%}
{%- else -%}
# run lint + typecheck + test, then e2e if runtime paths ({{ runtime_paths }}) changed
{%- endif %}
```

{% if e2e_cmd -%}
Check what changed before deciding on E2E:

```bash
git diff --name-only <default-branch>...HEAD
```

If a changed path matches `{{ runtime_paths }}`, the E2E suite **must** be green before any
"done". If not, skip E2E **explicitly** with a one-line justification naming the paths
touched. Same path criterion as CI — parity by review.

{% endif -%}
## Definition of done

- The full pipeline was run **after** the last change.
- Output is cited; exit code is 0; error/warning counts are zero.
- Only then may you commit, hand off, or report success.
